---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { AUTHOR, SITE, SOURCING_NOTE } from '../config';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
---
<Base title="About" description={`Who writes ${SITE.name}, and what experience the guides are based on.`}>
<div class="wrap"><Breadcrumbs trail={[{ label: "About", href: "/about/" }]} /></div>
<section class="wrap" style="padding:2rem 1.5rem 0">
  <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
  <h1 style="max-width:18ch">Who writes this</h1>
  <div class="prose" style="margin-top:2rem">
    <div style="display:flex;gap:1.2rem;align-items:center;margin-bottom:2rem">
      <div class="avatar" style="width:4.5rem;height:4.5rem;font-size:1.3rem" aria-hidden="true">{AUTHOR.initials}</div>
      <div>
        <h2 style="margin:0 0 .2rem">{AUTHOR.name}</h2>
        <p class="note" style="margin:0">{AUTHOR.role} &middot; {AUTHOR.company}</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p>{AUTHOR.bio}</p>
    <h2>Background</h2>
    <ul>{AUTHOR.credentials.map((c: string) => <li>{c}</li>)}</ul>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Role</th><th>Organisation</th><th>Period</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Founder</td><td>Independent e-commerce venture</td><td>2025&ndash;2026</td></tr>
        <tr><td>E-commerce specialist</td><td>Parknes Inc. &mdash; US e-commerce and 3PL</td><td>2024&ndash;2025</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <h2>What I do not claim</h2>
    <p>
      I am not a tax adviser, an accountant or a lawyer, and nothing here is professional advice. I do not
      currently operate the seller accounts described above, so figures drawn from that period are labelled
      with the period they cover rather than presented as current. Where a number is not mine, it is cited.
    </p>
    <h2>Why this site exists</h2>
    <p>
      Marketplace fee content has a specific failure mode. A number gets published without a date, another
      site repeats it, and eighteen months later sellers are pricing against a rate that no longer exists.
      During research for the guides here, four different published estimates were found for the same
      policy change — every one of them from a company selling the software that solves it.
    </p>
    <p>
      This site exists to do the boring part: go to the primary source, write down the date, name the
      publisher of every secondary figure, and say so when the sources disagree instead of picking one.
      {SOURCING_NOTE}
    </p>
    <p>
      What that means in practice is set out on the <a href="/how-we-test/">method page</a> and the{' '}
      <a href="/editorial-standards/">editorial standards page</a>, including a plain statement of which
      of the two sourcing routes each guide currently uses.
    </p>
    <h2>Publisher</h2>
    <p>{SITE.name} is published by <strong>{SITE.publisher}</strong>, an independent business with no ownership relationship to any marketplace or software vendor covered on this site.</p>
    <h2>How it is funded</h2>
    <p>
      Display advertising. Ads are served by third parties and have no influence on what we cover or
      how software is scored. There are no paid placements and no sponsored reviews.
    </p>
    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>Corrections and questions: <a href={`mailto:${AUTHOR.email}`}>{AUTHOR.email}</a>. Corrections are published on the <a href="/corrections/">corrections page</a>.</p>
  </div>
</section>
</Base>
